  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe are going to use a hybrid approach combining a global optimizer (Differential Evolution) and a local optimizer (SLSQP). The idea is to use DE to find a candidate solution that is globally promising, then use SLSQP to refine it to get a lower C5. DE helps escape local optima that the original SLSQP code had trouble with. This hybrid approach leverages the exploration power of DE with the exploitation power of SLSQP, ensuring we don't get stuck in poor local minima.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Objective function: \n    Let dx = 2.0 / n_points.\n    We define an objective function to be maximized by the original constraint, but here we minimize C5.\n    Specifically, we minimize C_5 = max_k integral h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx, but we use a smooth_max_obj function that approximates the max operation with a log-sum-exp barrier.\n\n- Constraint function: integral h(x) dx = 1, i.e., sum(h) * dx = 1, or sum(h) = n_points/2.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n- Predefined n_points = 85 (same as parent)\n- If initial_h_values is available, use it; else, use a random feasible point.\n\n- Define the objective function with a penalty for constraint violation:\n    def ob(x):\n        if abs(sum(x) - n_points/2) < 1e-5:\n            return smooth_max_obj(x)\n        else:\n            return smooth_max_obj(x) + 1e10 * abs(sum(x) - n_points/2)\n\n- Define the bounds for each variable: [0,1]\n\n- Use differential_evolution from scipy.optimize to find a candidate solution with:\n    - `bounds=[(0,1)]*n_points`\n    - `max_evaluations=50000`\n    - `mutation=(0.1, 0.5)`\n    - `recombination=0.5`\n    - `seed` parameter set to the provided seed\n    - `disp=True` to show progress (but optional in final code for speed)\n\n- After DE finds a candidate, use the best solution as initial for SLSQP optimization.\n\n4. Search choices and variations\n- We use n_points=85 to maintain consistent recovery plan.\n- DE will use 10000 function evaluations first for exploration.\n- Then SLSQP will refine from the DE's best candidate.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- DE: 10000 evals (assume 0.1s/eval \u2192 1000s)\n- SLSQP: 100 iterations (assume 0.1s/eval \u2192 10s)\n- Safety features: early exit if time budget exceeded, DE's max_evaluations should prevent excessive evaluations.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Validate:\n    - 0 <= x[i] <= 1 for all i\n    - Sum(x) \u2248 n_points/2 (within 1e-5)\n    - Objective is finite\n- Re-evaluate final solution from DE+SLSQP to ensure accuracy\n- Return structure: (h_values, c5_bound, n_points)",
